{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts","line":726,"code_snippet":"export function isLocalVoice(provider: string, modelId: string, trusted: TrustedConfig): boolean { ... return decl.modelGroups[modelId] === \"local\"; ... }","finding":"Under hounfour.locality: local_voices, Bridgebuilder's isLocalVoice/applyLocality decide locality from dispatch_group alone and never inspect the model entry's fallback_chain; cheval (chain_resolver.py:92) walks that chain inside one call, so a local voice whose chain names a hosted hop sends the PR content to a hosted provider when the local server fails.","reasoning_trace":"Read config.ts:722-751; compared with hop-locality.py:16-17,123-133 (fallback_chain_reaches_hosted) and bats LOC-7; confirmed Bridgebuilder voices dispatch via cheval-delegate.ts --model provider:model and that chain_resolver.py appends the primary's fallback_chain. Cross-model DISS-C-003 raised the same chain walk.","critique":"Three of four local_voices consumers honour the fallback-chain rule; Bridgebuilder does not.","remediation":"Parse models.<id>.fallback_chain into ProviderDecl and recurse in isLocalVoice (unresolved or non-local hop => hosted, depth-bounded), or shell out to hop-locality.py; add a trusted-config.test.ts case mirroring LOC-7.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html","https://owasp.org/Top10/A04_2021-Insecure_Design/"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/openai_adapter.py","line":217,"code_snippet":"def _transport_policy(self, model_config): if getattr(self.config, \"allow_insecure_endpoint\", None) or getattr(model_config, \"dispatch_group\", None) == \"local\": return TransportPolicy(...)","finding":"The D-7.2 request-time rules (no proxy env, no redirects, declared path prefix) are constructed only by OpenAIAdapter, while endpoint_policy.validate_providers admits allow_insecure_endpoint and dispatch_group: local for any non-CLI provider type; anthropic/google adapters call http_post/http_post_stream/http_get without policy.","reasoning_trace":"base.py:270,378,468 policy param optional; grep of anthropic_adapter.py/google_adapter.py shows no policy argument; endpoint_policy.py:153-156 checks type only via _is_cli_provider.","critique":"Documented guarantee (endpoint_policy.py:26-28) holds for one adapter family.","remediation":"Refuse the opt-in / dispatch_group local at load for provider types whose adapter lacks the policy, or build the policy in ProviderAdapter so every adapter gets it; add a load test for the refused shape.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/skills/bridgebuilder-review/resources/config.ts","line":669,"code_snippet":"// Head-only refusal: on a PR the head checkout is attacker-controlled. ... keylessOnlyInHead || insecureOnlyInHead","finding":"The trusted-configuration layer (D-7.5) refuses head-only keyless/insecure declarations but never compares endpoint or auth; every voice dispatches through cheval, which loads the checkout's .loa.config.yaml and (endpoint-validator.py:1291) admits any declared https host, so a PR head can repoint a credentialed built-in provider at a host it controls and the key plus the diff are sent there. Pre-existing exposure; the new mitigation leaves it open while README/SKILL.md describe providers as read from trusted config only.","reasoning_trace":"config.ts:605-712 (trusted view = keyless, insecure, authEnv, dispatch groups only); cheval-delegate.ts:146 passes --model to cheval; loader.py:704 validate_providers -> validate_declared_endpoint skips step 8 allowlist; SKILL.md:116-118 notes the shipped model has no PR-head checkout. Cross-model DISS-C-005 raised the allowlist omission.","critique":"Mitigation is incomplete for the threat model it states.","remediation":"Have Bridgebuilder pass the trusted provider block to cheval (e.g. a config override path) or refuse a voice whose head endpoint/auth differ from the trusted declaration; on the cheval side WARN or refuse when a credentialed ({env:}) provider's https host is outside the canonical allowlist unless declared in a user/system layer.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/522.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"consistency","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/lib/hop-locality.py","line":116,"code_snippet":"group = entry.get(\"dispatch_group\") or block.get(\"dispatch_group\") or \"\"","finding":"Three definitions of local: the planners (hop-locality.py:116, config.ts:730-732) accept a provider-level dispatch_group or all-models-local, cheval's loader requires the model-level key (loader.py _validate_model_auth_metadata) and ModelConfig/MODELINV read only the model entry (cheval.py:541, modelinv.py:473-475).","reasoning_trace":"Read all three readers; the review reproduced CONFIG-INVALID for a provider-level-only key. Cross-model DISS-C-004.","critique":"A hop can be planned local, refused by cheval at load, and recorded hosted in MODELINV.","remediation":"Drop the provider-block rule from both planners (model-level only) or make cheval honour it everywhere.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py","line":151,"code_snippet":"optin = prov.get(\"allow_insecure_endpoint\") ... check_endpoint(endpoint, optin, name)","finding":"allow_insecure_endpoint is independent of keyless: a provider with an http RFC1918 endpoint and auth: {env:VAR} loads and the adapter sends the Bearer credential in cleartext (openai_adapter.py:172-173); no WARN at load.","reasoning_trace":"validate_providers couples nothing; the example config (.loa.config.yaml.example:1235-1237) explicitly invites a keyed local server. Cross-model DISS-C-001.","critique":"Operator-chosen, loopback/RFC1918 only, but silent.","remediation":"WARN (or refuse) at load when an opted-in http provider is not keyless, and name the env var.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/providers/openai_adapter.py","line":101,"code_snippet":"return \"response_format\" in text or \"json_schema\" in text","finding":"The schema-rejection heuristic is a substring scan of the whole HTTP 400 body; any 400 whose text mentions response_format/json_schema (including an echoed prompt) triggers one retry without the schema, so the server can downgrade enforcement and double the request; recorded in telemetry only.","reasoning_trace":"openai_adapter.py:94-111, 190-204. Cross-model DISS-C-002.","critique":"Same destination, recorded, but server-driven.","remediation":"Match the structured error (error.param == response_format / error.code unsupported_parameter) and surface schema_rejected_by_server to the caller.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/757.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":551,"code_snippet":"if _optin_raw is not None: _optin = _check_endpoint(...) if prov.get(\"endpoint\") else None","finding":"The defence-in-depth re-check in _build_provider_config runs only when an opt-in is present; a hand-built config with an http/loopback endpoint and no opt-in reaches ProviderConfig unchecked, and a lone opt-in with no endpoint is not validated.","reasoning_trace":"cheval.py:546-557; load_config is the real gate (loader.py:704). Cross-model DISS-C-006.","critique":"Gap only matters when load_config is bypassed.","remediation":"Call check_endpoint unconditionally for non-CLI providers with an endpoint; validate a lone opt-in via canonical_optin_host.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-007","category":"security","criterion":"info_disclosure","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/loa_cheval/config/endpoint_policy.py","line":200,"code_snippet":"\"endpoint\": prov.get(\"endpoint\") or \"\",","finding":"describe-provider prints the post-interpolation endpoint verbatim and _main prints str(exc) on load failure (line 224); the probe logs the URL (model-health-probe.sh:1505). interpolate_config is eager for every string except providers.*.auth, so an endpoint template embedding {env:TOKEN} leaks the value into probe logs/CI output.","reasoning_trace":"interpolation.py:40 _DEFAULT_LAZY_PATHS; endpoint_policy.py:184-206,224. Cross-model DISS-C-007.","critique":"Docstring says never carries a secret.","remediation":"Emit scheme/host/port via split_url as destination_for does; redact load errors.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/532.html"]}
{"id":"OPS-001","category":"devops","criterion":"consistency","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/model-health-probe.sh","line":1469,"code_snippet":"local _vflags=(--json --allowlist \"$PROBE_PROVIDERS_ALLOWLIST\")","finding":"_probe_configured validates a configured provider's /models URL with the host allowlist, while cheval admits an operator-declared https host via validate_declared_endpoint; a hosted open-weight API that loads in cheval is answered UNKNOWN / endpoint_refused by the probe.","reasoning_trace":"model-health-probe.sh:1468-1481 vs endpoint-validator.py:1080-1087.","critique":"Named refusal, not silent.","remediation":"Pass a declared-endpoint mode to the validator CLI for configured providers, or document the allowlist requirement.","confidence":"medium","references":[]}
{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"complexity","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/model-health-probe.sh","line":1428,"code_snippet":"_probe_configured() { ... }","finding":"_probe_configured (~110 lines, four repeated early-return blocks), loadTrustedConfig (config.ts:605, ~105 lines) and _adv_advisory_block (adversarial-review.sh:3972, ~65 lines with a 30-line embedded jq program) exceed the 50-line threshold without a justification comment.","reasoning_trace":"Line counts from pr/head files.","critique":"Readability of the security-relevant probe and trusted-config paths.","remediation":"Extract _probe_unknown helper; split PR-mode source resolution; move the jq program to a .jq file.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
{"id":"DOC-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"documentation","severity":"LOW","score":3,"file":"head/README.md","line":22,"code_snippet":"**Unreleased — earned guards and open voices** (cycle-129, [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md)):","finding":"The implementation report (pr/PR.md) has no AC Verification walkthrough or test evidence; the README points at a CHANGELOG entry that is not in the diff, so the security changes (endpoint opt-in, trusted config, exit codes) cannot be confirmed as logged; no documentation-coherence subagent reports exist.","reasoning_trace":"pr/PR.md is two lines; pr/head/CHANGELOG.md absent; grimoires/loa/a2a/subagent-reports absent.","critique":"Reviewer and auditor must re-derive everything.","remediation":"Add the AC walkthrough and test commands to reviewer.md; include the CHANGELOG entry (or its commit) in the change set.","confidence":"high","references":[]}
{"id":"SUMMARY","category":"security","criterion":"summary","severity":"INFO","score":3,"finding":"sprint-1 audit of pr/head.diff: critical 0, high 1, medium 2, low 8; verdict CHANGES_REQUIRED. Rubric: SEC-IV 4, SEC-AZ 3, SEC-CI 3, SEC-IN 5, SEC-AV 4; ARCH 3; CQ 3; DEVOPS 4.","reasoning_trace":"Tally per Phase 2.5 of auditor-sprint-feedback.md; dissent envelope grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-audit.json (2 independent voices, 7 findings, 0 rejected, not degraded).","confidence":"high"}

