{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/.claude/adapters/cheval.py","line":551,"code_snippet":"if _optin_raw is not None: _optin = _check_endpoint(...) if prov.get(\"endpoint\") else None","finding":"The defence-in-depth re-check in _build_provider_config runs only when an opt-in is present; a hand-built config with an http/loopback endpoint and no opt-in reaches ProviderConfig unchecked, and a lone opt-in with no endpoint is not validated.","reasoning_trace":"cheval.py:546-557; load_config is the real gate (loader.py:704). Cross-model DISS-C-006.","critique":"Gap only matters when load_config is bypassed.","remediation":"Call check_endpoint unconditionally for non-CLI providers with an endpoint; validate a lone opt-in via canonical_optin_host.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html"]}
